      "description": "Watch AC Milan vs Venezia highlights and goals from Serie A on ReFooty: Football Highlights Hub. Match played on August 28, 2026. A tactical stalemate at San Siro On August 28, 2026, AC Milan and Venezia collided at the iconic San Siro in a Serie A fixture that promised a compelling display of tactical awareness. Both sides approached the match with caution, making it clear from the opening whistle that space would be at a premium throughout the ninety minutes. The flow of the game Throughout the first half, the battle was largely fought in the middle of the park. AC Milan sought to unlock the defense through the creative passing of Luka Modric , while the Venezia backline remained disciplined, albeit aggressive, picking up early cautions for tactical fouls. The defensive nature of the encounter meant that chances were rare, forcing both teams to rely on set-pieces and moments of individual brilliance to spark a goal . Breaking the deadlock momentum shifted significantly in the second half following a flurry of substitutions. The breakthrough finally arrived in the 69th minute when Goncalo Ramos capitalized on a clever assist from Alexis Saelemaekers , firing a left-footed strike into the net to give the home side the advantage. The goal forced Venezia to push forward, but the intensity of the match only increased as the visitors searched for an equalizer. Late drama concludes the tie Just as the game seemed to be settling into a predictable rhythm, disaster struck for the visitors. In the 89th minute, an unfortunate defensive blunder led to an own goal by Redouane Halhal , shifting the outcome of the contest. Despite a late push by Venezia during the four minutes of stoppage time, featuring corner kicks from Gianluca Busio , the AC Milan defense stood tall to secure a hard-fought result in this sports encounter."
